Feature: Data Validation for Unity Catalog Schema 'purgo_playground'

  Background:
    Given a sample sales data file "sample_sales_data.csv" exists with columns:
      | country_cd   | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |

  Scenario Outline: Validate data entries in the sales data
    Given the sales data file is loaded
    When validating the data entries for <column>
    Then the data <should|should not> conform to the format rules:
      | column     | format                                |
      | country_cd | Non-empty String, length 2            |
      | product_id | Starts with 'P', followed by 4 digits |
      | qty_sold   | Integer, greater than 0              |
      | sales_date | YYYY-MM-DD, valid date               |

    Examples:
      | column     | should      |
      | country_cd | should      |
      | product_id | should      |
      | qty_sold   | should      |
      | sales_date | should      |

  Scenario: Check missing fields in schema
    Given the schema 'purgo_playground' is proposed
    When reviewing the design
    Then the following requirements must be addressed:
      | Requirement                           |
      | Purpose and objectives                |
      | Data flow and integration points      |
      | User roles and access control         |
      | Data processing or transformations    |
      | Expected outputs or reports           |
      | Data update frequency and methods     |
      | Project timeline and milestones       |

  Scenario Outline: Validate error scenarios for incorrect data
    Given a row has <error_condition>
    When processing the data entry
    Then an error message should be displayed: <error_message>

    Examples:
      | error_condition                | error_message                        |
      | missing country code           | "Error: Country code is required"    |
      | invalid product ID format      | "Error: Product ID must start with 'P' followed by 4 digits" |
      | negative quantity sold         | "Error: Quantity sold must be positive" |
      | invalid date format            | "Error: Date must be in format YYYY-MM-DD" |

  Scenario: Validate accessibility and roles
    Given the schema 'purgo_playground' will be developed
    When defining roles and access levels
    Then the following roles should have access with conditions:
      | Role          | Access Level               |
      | Data Analyst  | Read-only                  |
      | Data Engineer | Read-write for integration |
      | Admin         | Full access                |

  Scenario: Ensure data update frequency compliance
    Given the sales data is updated regularly
    When defining update frequencies
    Then the schema should support data updates every <frequency> using <method>

    Examples:
      | frequency | method             |
      | daily     | Scheduled batch    |
      | real-time | Streaming updates  |

  Scenario: Define expected outputs from the schema
    Given the schema 'purgo_playground' is used for analysis
    When generating reports
    Then the following outputs should be expected:
      | Output             |
      | Sales by country   |
      | Sales by product   |
      | Total sales summary|

  Scenario: Integration with existing systems
    Given the schema needs to integrate with existing systems
    When designing integration points
    Then it should support data flow compatibility with:
      | System          |
      | Data Warehouse  |
      | ETL pipelines   |
      | Reporting tools |

  Scenario: Identify and include milestones in project timeline
    Given the implementation roadmap
    When planning the project
    Then include critical milestones such as:
      | Milestone                        |
      | Schema design completion         |
      | Initial data integration         |
      | First report generation          |
      | Go-live                          |

